From: jikiservant-cmyk <253226408+jikiservant-cmyk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:04:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(billing): fail closed on unregistered payment-type codes;
 seed BUY_SMS
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The create-payment route resolved an unknown paymentTypeCode to NULL and,
because isPlatformPayment requires a resolved type, booked the payment as a
TENANT collection. For Kunity's BUY_SMS code (a platform fee in
PLATFORM_FEE_TYPES) that silently routed a platform fee into the tenant's
provider float while the SMS credits were still granted — the exact
mis-billing mode found in the Kunity-NaJiki contract review.

- POST /api/payments now rejects a supplied-but-unregistered paymentTypeCode
  with 400 and an operator-actionable message, decided by the pure
  src/lib/payment-type-guard.ts helper.
- scripts/seed.ts registers BUY_SMS for the sacco application, so a fresh
  install bills SMS bundles through the platform account out of the box.
- The seeded sacco application webhookPath now points at Kunity's real
  notification listener (/api/webhooks/najiki); the previous placeholder path
  exists in no Kunity deployment and would have dropped every notification.

tests/payment-type-guard.test.ts covers the rejection, message contract, the
registered-code and legacy (no-code) pass-throughs. npm test: 153 passed,
0 failed. tsc reports no new errors (pre-existing data.ts drift is unchanged).
